            "Suppose the university newspaper is inviting submissions from the students for its coming edition on future applications of robots on campus. You are now to write an essay for submission. You will have 30 minutes to write the essay. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.",
          promptZh:
            "假设校报正在征稿，下一期主题为“机器人在校园中的未来应用”。请你写一篇应征短文。",
          modelEssay: `Nowadays, robots are no longer a scene from science fiction; they are quietly entering our campuses. In the near future, I believe they will play three major roles in university life.

To begin with, robots can take over repetitive chores. Delivery robots have already carried parcels and meals across some campuses, saving students valuable time. In addition, library robots could help sort books and guide readers to the right shelves. More importantly, robots may support learning: a robot assistant can answer routine questions, while language learners practise conversations with it without feeling embarrassed.

However, I do not think robots will replace human contact. Campus life is built on communication between people, and machines should serve that goal rather than dominate it. Privacy and safety must also be carefully protected.

In short, robots will make campus life more efficient and convenient, but only if we use them wisely and keep people at the centre.`,
