          promptEn:
            "Suppose it is proposed that university students should be required to participate in at least one research project. You are now to write a response by stating what you think of the proposal in terms of its necessity and practicality. You will have 30 minutes to write the response. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.",
          promptZh:
            "假设有人提议：大学生必须至少参与一项科研项目。请从必要性和可行性两个角度，写一篇短文表达你的看法。",
          modelEssay: `Nowadays, research ability is increasingly valued in higher education. Some people propose that university students should be required to take part in at least one research project. From my perspective, this proposal has its necessity in terms of ability cultivation, but its practicality remains questionable.

For one thing, the requirement is necessary. Research projects enable students to apply theoretical knowledge to real problems, which helps develop their critical thinking and problem-solving skills. These abilities will benefit them a lot in future job hunting or further study. For another, its practicality is not ideal. Not all students are interested in or suitable for academic research. Forcing them to participate may lead to perfunctory work. Besides, limited faculty and resources can hardly support high-quality guidance for every student.

To sum up, it is more advisable to encourage rather than require students to join research projects. Universities can provide more accessible research opportunities for those who are willing to explore academic fields.`,
          modelEssayZh:
            "如今，科研能力在高等教育中越来越受重视。有人提议，应要求大学生至少参与一项科研项目。在我看来，这一提议从能力培养的角度有其必要性，但可行性仍存疑问。一方面，这项要求有其必要性。科研项目能让学生将理论知识应用于实际问题，有助于培养批判性思维和解决问题的能力，这些能力对今后求职或深造都大有裨益。另一方面，其可行性并不理想。并非所有学生都对学术研究感兴趣或适合做研究，强迫参与可能导致敷衍了事；此外，有限的师资和资源也难以给每位学生提供高质量指导。总之，鼓励而非强制学生参与科研项目更为明智。高校可以为愿意探索学术领域的学生提供更多易获得的机会。",
