          id: "translation-3",
          type: "translation",
          title: "Part IV 翻译",
          short: "翻译",
          minutes: 30,
          original: `餐桌礼仪（dining etiquette）是中华传统文化的重要组成部分，蕴含着热情有礼的待客之道。为了招待客人，主人会根据客人的口味和喜好准备丰富精致的菜肴。就餐座位的安排非常讲究，主人坐在正对大门的位置，在主人身边就座的是最重要的客人。进餐时，主人会不时地为客人添酒加菜。这种独特的餐桌礼仪已延续了数千年，对促进和谐的人际交往起到了重要作用。`,
          reference: `Dining etiquette is an important part of traditional Chinese culture, embodying the hospitality and courtesy with which Chinese people treat guests. To entertain guests, the host will prepare a rich and exquisite selection of dishes according to the guests' tastes and preferences. The seating arrangement is particularly meticulous: the host sits directly facing the door, and the most honored guest sits next to the host. During the meal, the host will from time to time refill the guests' wine glasses and serve more food. This distinctive dining etiquette has been passed down for thousands of years and plays a significant role in fostering harmonious interpersonal relationships.`,
