        "promptEn": "Suppose your university is conducting a survey to collect students' opinions on the appropriate use of AI technology in assisting learning. You are now to write an essay to express your view. You will have 30 minutes for the task. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.",
        "promptZh": "学校调查学生对恰当使用AI技术辅助学习的看法，请写文章表达你的观点。",
        "modelEssay": "In my view, AI technology, when used appropriately, is a valuable ally in learning rather than a shortcut that replaces genuine effort. Since our university is surveying students on this issue, I would like to voice my support for embracing AI in a sensible, balanced way.\n\nThere are solid reasons for this position. First, AI tools raise learning efficiency: a chatbot can explain a confusing grammar point instantly, check my essay for mistakes, or gather background material that once took hours in the library. Second, AI offers personalized tutoring, adjusting its explanations to my own pace and weak spots. Admittedly, however, over-reliance is a real danger; if students let AI think for them, their own analytical skills will gradually wither.\n\nTherefore, the key lies in \"appropriate\" use. We should treat AI as an assistant that guides and inspires, not a machine that hands us ready-made answers. Used within this boundary, AI can truly make learning smarter.",
        "modelEssayZh": "在我看来，只要使用得当，人工智能技术就是学习中的得力伙伴，而不是替代真正努力的捷径。既然我们学校正就这一问题向学生征集意见，我愿表达自己的支持——以理性、平衡的方式拥抱AI。\n持这一立场有充分的理由。首先，AI工具能提升学习效率：聊天机器人能即刻讲清一个绕人的语法点，帮我检查作文里的错误，或者找来过去要在图书馆花上几个小时才能找到的背景资料。其次，AI能提供个性化辅导，按我自己的节奏和薄弱环节来调整它的讲解。不过，必须承认，过度依赖是真实存在的危险；如果学生让AI替自己思考，他们自身的分析能力就会逐渐退化。\n因此，关键在于「合理」使用。我们应把AI当作引导和启发我们的助手，而不是直接递给我们现成答案的机器。在这条边界之内使用，AI才能真正让学习变得更聪明。",
