        "promptEn": "Suppose your university is seeking students' opinions on the necessity of making College Chinese a compulsory course. You are now to write an essay to express your view. You will have 30 minutes for the task. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.",
        "promptZh": "学校就大学语文是否应设为必修课征集学生意见，请写文章表达你的观点。",
        "modelEssay": "The question of whether College Chinese should be a compulsory course has sparked heated discussion on campus. In my view, making it compulsory is both necessary and wise.\n\nAdmittedly, some students argue that Chinese is their mother tongue and needs no further study. Yet this view overlooks two facts. First, a solid command of Chinese sharpens our thinking and expression. Many science majors write reports full of grammatical errors and muddled logic, which weakens their careers. A required course would help them communicate clearly. What's more, classical Chinese carries our cultural heritage. Through reading poems and essays, students inherit values and a sense of identity that no other subject offers.\n\nTherefore, I firmly believe College Chinese deserves a place as a compulsory course. It is not a burden but an investment in both our language ability and our cultural roots.",
        "modelEssayZh": "大学语文是否应设为一门必修课，在校园里引发了热烈讨论。在我看来，把它设为必修既必要又明智。\n诚然，有些学生认为中文是母语，无需再学。然而这种看法忽视了两点事实。第一，扎实的中文功底能磨练我们的思维与表达。许多理工科学生写出的报告满是语法错误、逻辑混乱，这会拖累他们的职业发展。一门必修课能帮助他们清晰地沟通。此外，古典中文承载着我们的文化遗产。通过阅读诗文，学生得以传承价值观与身份认同，这是任何其他学科都给不了的。\n因此，我坚信大学语文理应占据一门必修课的位置。它不是负担，而是对我们语言能力与文化根脉的一项投资。",
