        "promptEn": "Suppose the university newspaper is inviting submissions from the students for its coming edition on how the students can contribute to a green campus. You are now to write an essay for submission. You will have 30 minutes to write the essay. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.",
        "promptZh": "校报征稿：学生如何为绿色校园贡献力量，请写一篇文章投稿。",
        "modelEssay": "A green campus is no longer a slogan but a shared responsibility, and students play a key role in making it real. As members of the campus, we can turn small daily habits into real changes.\n\nThere are several practical things we can do. First, we should sort our rubbish and recycle paper, bottles and cans, which cuts waste and saves resources. Second, saving water and switching off lights and computers when they are not in use can greatly reduce the energy our campus consumes. Moreover, choosing to walk, cycle or share bikes for short trips lowers carbon emissions, and passing used textbooks on to younger students gives them a second life instead of being thrown away.\n\nIn short, a green campus grows out of these everyday actions rather than empty talk. If every student takes one small step, our campus will surely become cleaner, greener and more livable for us all.",
        "modelEssayZh": "绿色校园不再是一句口号，而是一份共同的责任，学生在把它变为现实的过程中扮演着关键角色。作为校园的一员，我们能把日常的小习惯变成真正的改变。\n我们能做的实事有好几件。第一，我们应当对垃圾进行分类，回收纸张、瓶子和易拉罐，这既减少了浪费，也节约了资源。第二，节约用水、在不使用时随手关掉电灯和电脑，能大大降低校园的能耗。此外，短途出行选择步行、骑车或共享单车能减少碳排放，而把用过的教材传给学弟学妹，则让它们获得第二次生命，而不是被扔掉。\n总之，绿色校园源于这些日常的行动，而非空谈。只要每个学生都迈出一小步，我们的校园必将变得更干净、更绿色，也更宜居，让我们所有人受益。",
