        "modelEssay": "Recently, our university has been collecting opinions on whether campus canteens should welcome outside visitors. In my view, opening them to the public is a wise move that benefits both the campus and the community.\n\nFor one thing, university canteens usually offer clean and affordable meals, so opening them can relieve the dining pressure faced by nearby residents and office workers who struggle to find cheap lunches. For another, the extra income earned from these visitors allows canteens to upgrade their equipment and even lower prices for students. Admittedly, more diners may cause crowding and raise safety concerns; however, such problems can be eased by setting fixed visiting hours and checking visitors at the gate.\n\nTherefore, I firmly believe that a properly managed open canteen is worthwhile. As long as student needs come first, sharing this resource makes our university a warmer part of society.",
        "modelEssayZh": "最近，我校正在征集大家对『校园食堂是否应向公众开放』的意见。在我看来，向公众开放是明智之举，校园和社区双方都能从中受益。\n一方面，高校食堂通常提供干净又实惠的餐食，开放后能缓解附近居民和上班族的就餐压力，他们往往很难找到便宜的午餐。另一方面，外来就餐者带来的额外收入能让食堂升级设备，甚至为学生降低菜价。诚然，就餐人数增多可能造成拥挤、带来安全隐患；但这些问题可以通过设定固定开放时段、在门口对访客进行登记来缓解。\n因此，我坚信一个管理得当的开放食堂是值得的。只要学生的需求被放在首位，共享这一资源就能让我们的学校成为社会中更温暖的一部分。",
