        "promptEn": "Suppose your university is seeking students’ opinions on whether university libraries should be open to the public. You are now to write an essay to express your view. You will have 30 minutes for the task. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.",
        "promptZh": "学校就『大学图书馆是否应向公众开放』征求意见，写短文表达你的观点，120—180词。",
        "modelEssay": "Whether university libraries should open their doors to the public has sparked heated debate in recent years. In my view, these libraries should indeed be accessible to ordinary citizens, provided that reasonable management measures are in place.\n\nTwo reasons support my position. Firstly, opening university libraries promotes the sharing of knowledge. Many valuable books and academic resources sit idle on the shelves, and allowing the public to use them turns campus libraries into vibrant centers of lifelong learning. Moreover, such openness enriches the cultural life of the whole community. For instance, a retired worker or a curious teenager could freely explore fields they never studied at school, which narrows the gap between universities and society.\n\nAdmittedly, outside visitors may strain limited seats and disturb students. Yet this problem can be eased by setting fixed visiting hours and registration rules. Therefore, I firmly believe university libraries should welcome the public, so long as students' study needs are fully protected.",
        "modelEssayZh": "近年来，大学图书馆是否应向公众开放，引发了热烈讨论。在我看来，这些图书馆确实应当向普通市民开放，前提是要有合理的管理措施。\n有两条理由支撑我的立场。首先，开放大学图书馆能促进知识共享。许多有价值的图书和学术资源在书架上闲置，让公众使用它们，能把校园图书馆变成充满活力的终身学习场所。此外，这样的开放能丰富整个社区的文化生活。例如，一位退休工人或一个好奇的少年，可以自由探索他们从未在学校学过的领域，从而缩小大学与社会之间的距离。\n诚然，外来访客可能会挤占有限的座位、打扰在校生。但这一问题可以通过设定固定的开放时段和登记制度来缓解。因此，我坚定地认为，只要在校生的学习需求得到充分保障，大学图书馆就应当欢迎公众进入。",
