        "promptEn": "Suppose the university newspaper is inviting submissions from the students for its coming edition on what in their university impresses them most.You are now to write an essay for submission. You will have 30 minutes to write the essay. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.",
        "promptZh": "假定校报就『大学里最令你印象深刻的是什么』向学生征稿，写一篇投稿短文，120—180词。",
        "modelEssay": "Among the many things on campus, it is the university library that has impressed me most. While my college offers modern labs and lively clubs, none of them stays in my heart as deeply as that quiet building.\n\nQuiet and well-lit, the library offers a space where I can truly focus and lose myself in books. Surrounded by towering shelves, I felt the joy of learning for the very first time. What touched me even more was a small experience. I still remember the day when I was searching desperately for an out-of-print book. It was a gentle old librarian who spent half an hour helping me track it down, which made me realize that this place is warmed not only by knowledge but also by kindness.\n\nLooking back, the library is more than a study room; it has taught me to seek knowledge actively rather than passively. That is why this quiet corner will always be the most unforgettable part of my university life.",
        "modelEssayZh": "在校园众多事物之中，最让我印象深刻的是学校图书馆。尽管我的大学有现代化的实验室和活跃的社团，但没有一样像那座安静的楼那样深深留在我心里。\n图书馆安静而明亮，给了我一个能真正专注、徜徉书海的空间。被高耸的书架环绕着，我第一次体会到学习的快乐。更让我感动的是一件小事。我仍记得那天，我焦急地到处找一本绝版书。是一位和蔼的老馆员花了半个小时帮我把它找到，这让我意识到，这个地方不仅被知识温暖着，也被善意温暖着。\n回想起来，图书馆不只是一个自习室；它教会我主动而非被动地去求知。这就是为什么这个安静的角落将永远是我大学生活中最难忘的部分。",
