        "promptEn": "Suppose you have attended a lecture delivered by a famous scholar. Write a report to the campus newspaper, summarizing its most important points. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.",
        "promptZh": "给校报写一篇报道，总结一位知名学者讲座的最重要的内容。",
        "modelEssay": "A Report on Professor Li's Lecture\n\nLast week our university had the honor of hosting a lecture by Professor Li, a well-known scholar in education, who spoke to a full hall of students on how to grow during our college years.\n\nThe speaker raised several important points. First, he pointed out that lifelong learning is the key to coping with a rapidly changing world, arguing that the knowledge we gain today may soon be out of date. He went on to emphasize that we should turn our curiosity into action and never be afraid of making mistakes, since real growth comes from trying rather than waiting. To illustrate this, he cited his own failures as the most valuable lessons in his career.\n\nThe lecture was warmly received, and many students felt newly inspired to take charge of their own learning. In short, it offered all of us valuable insight into making the most of our college life.",
        "modelEssayZh": "李教授讲座报道\n上周，我校有幸举办了一场由李教授主讲的讲座。李教授是教育领域一位知名学者，他面对座无虚席的同学，谈了我们应如何在大学阶段实现成长。\n主讲人提出了几个重要观点。第一，他指出终身学习是应对快速变化世界的关键，并认为我们今天学到的知识可能很快就会过时。接着他强调，我们应把好奇心转化为行动，永远不要害怕犯错，因为真正的成长源于尝试而非等待。为说明这一点，他举了自己的失败经历，称那是职业生涯中最宝贵的教训。\n这场讲座广受欢迎，许多同学倍受鼓舞，决心主动掌握自己的学习。总之，它让我们所有人都对如何充分利用大学生活有了宝贵的领悟。",
