        "id": "writing-2023-03-2",
        "type": "writing",
        "title": "Part I 写作",
        "short": "写作",
        "minutes": 30,
        "promptEn": "Suppose you have read a book recently and intend to recommend it to other members of your book club via an online forum. Briefly introduce the book and explain why it is worth reading. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.",
        "promptZh": "在读书会线上论坛发帖，简要介绍一本书并说明其值得一读的理由。",
        "modelEssay": "I'd like to recommend a book that truly moved me to all of you in our book club. It is Everything I Never Told You, written by Celeste Ng. The novel tells the story of a mixed-race family struggling with expectations, silence and the search for who they really are.\n\nThere are two reasons why I think it is worth reading. First, what impressed me most is how the book makes you rethink the way we express love and expectations within a family. It taught me that unspoken pressure can hurt the people we care about, instead of simply being an \"interesting\" story. What's more, the characters' loneliness and quiet struggles feel so real, which makes the novel easy to relate to, and the plain, honest language never gets boring.\n\nIf you are looking for a book that touches your heart and makes you think, I highly recommend that you give it a read. I'm sure it will stay with you, and I'd love to hear your thoughts on the forum.",
        "modelEssayZh": "我想向我们书友会的各位推荐一本真正打动我的书。它是伍绮诗所著的《无声告白》。这部小说讲述了一个混血家庭在期望、沉默以及对真实自我的追寻中挣扎的故事。\n我认为它值得一读有两个理由。第一，最打动我的是这本书会让你重新思考我们在家庭中表达爱与期望的方式。它让我懂得：没有说出口的压力会伤害我们所在乎的人，而不仅仅是一个『有意思』的故事。此外，书中人物的孤独与无声的挣扎是那样真实，让人很容易产生共鸣，而朴实、真诚的语言也从不令人厌倦。\n如果你在找一本既触动心灵又引人思考的书，我强烈推荐你读一读。我相信它会久久留在你心里，也很期待在论坛上听到你的想法。",
