        "promptEn": "Suppose you have taken part in a career planning seminar. Write an account of the seminar and summarize what you have learned from it. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.",
        "promptZh": "写一篇短文，记述你参加的职业生涯规划讲座并总结从中获得的收获。",
        "modelEssay": "Last week, our university held a career planning seminar in the lecture hall, which attracted a large number of students who are about to face job hunting. The lecture was delivered by an experienced human resources manager, who has helped many graduates find suitable jobs.\n\nDuring the seminar, the speaker focused on how to plan a career and pointed out that many graduates feel lost simply because they have never planned ahead. He suggested that we should first recognize our own interests and strengths, then set clear and realistic goals, and finally start to build up relevant skills as early as possible. What impressed me most was a real story about a student who got an ideal offer through years of careful preparation.\n\nThis seminar made me realize that career planning should never be put off until graduation. From now on, I will think seriously about what I really want and take small steps toward my goals instead of drifting along. After all, a well-planned future begins with action today.",
        "modelEssayZh": "上周，我们学校在阶梯教室举办了一场职业规划讲座，吸引了大批即将面临求职的同学。讲座由一位经验丰富的人力资源经理主讲，他曾帮助许多毕业生找到合适的工作。\n讲座中，主讲人重点讲了如何规划职业，并指出许多毕业生之所以感到迷茫，仅仅是因为他们从未提前规划。他建议我们首先认清自己的兴趣与长处，然后设定清晰而现实的目标，最后尽早开始积累相关技能。让我印象最深的是一个真实故事：一位学生通过多年精心准备拿到了理想的录用通知。\n这场讲座让我意识到，职业规划绝不应拖到毕业才做。从现在起，我会认真思考自己真正想要什么，并朝目标一步步前进，而不是随波逐流。毕竟，规划良好的未来始于今天的行动。",
