        "promptEn": "For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write an essay titled “Doviolent video games lead to violence?”. The statement given below is for your reference. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words .\nA growing body of research finds that violent video games can make kids act aggressively in their real world relationships, causing an increase in violence.",
        "promptZh": "就「暴力电子游戏是否导致现实暴力」写一篇短文，表明并论证自己的立场。",
        "modelEssay": "Do violent video games lead to violence? While a growing body of research suggests such games can make players more aggressive, I believe they do not directly cause real violence; rather, their influence depends on the individual and the surrounding environment.\n\nTo begin with, exposure to violent scenes may indeed shape behavior. First, children who spend hours shooting and fighting on screen can gradually treat aggression as normal, and some may copy what they see when they lose their temper. However, most players clearly separate games from reality. A well-supervised teenager, for instance, can enjoy an action game after homework and still behave kindly toward classmates, because family guidance and self-control matter far more than the game itself.\n\nIn conclusion, violent video games alone do not turn ordinary people into violent ones. What truly counts is proper parental supervision and healthy habits. Therefore, rather than simply blaming the games, parents and schools should teach children to play in moderation and to tell fantasy from real life.",
        "modelEssayZh": "暴力电子游戏会导致暴力吗？虽然越来越多的研究表明这类游戏可能让玩家更具攻击性，但我认为它们并不会直接导致现实中的暴力；相反，其影响取决于玩家个体以及周围的环境。\n首先，接触暴力画面确实可能塑造行为。第一，那些花大量时间在屏幕上射击、打斗的孩子，可能渐渐把攻击视为常态，有些人在发脾气时会模仿所见。然而，大多数玩家能清楚地把游戏和现实分开。举例来说，一个受到良好监管的青少年，可以在写完作业后享受一款动作游戏，却依旧待同学友善，因为家庭引导和自控远比游戏本身更重要。\n总之，暴力电子游戏本身并不会把普通人变成施暴者。真正起作用的是恰当的家长监管和健康的习惯。因此，与其一味归咎于游戏，家长和学校更应教孩子适度游戏，并学会分清虚构与现实。",
