        "promptEn": "For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write an essay titled“Is technology making people lazy?”.The statement given below is for your reference. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words .\nMany studies claim that computers distract people, make them lazy thinkers and even lower their work efficiency.",
        "promptZh": "就「科技是否使人变懒」这一话题写一篇短文，给出观点并加以论证。",
        "modelEssay": "Is technology making people lazy? My answer is a qualified yes: while technology itself is neutral, the way most of us use it does breed laziness of both mind and body.\n\nTo begin with, technology encourages mental laziness. When a search engine can answer any question in seconds and a navigation app can guide every turn, few people bother to think, memorize or reason on their own. Gradually, we outsource our brains and lose the habit of deep thinking. Physical laziness follows the same logic: with delivery apps and online services, many people rarely walk, cook or move, so their bodies grow as idle as their minds.\n\nAdmittedly, technology can also make us more efficient. Yet the tool is not to blame; our passive dependence is. Therefore, the real question is not whether technology makes us lazy, but whether we control it or let it control us. Used wisely, it frees us; used blindly, it enslaves us.",
        "modelEssayZh": "科技正在让人变懒吗？我的回答是有条件的肯定：科技本身是中性的，但我们大多数人使用它的方式，确实滋生了思维和身体两方面的懒惰。\n首先，科技助长思维上的懒惰。当搜索引擎几秒就能回答任何问题、导航软件能指引每一个转弯时，很少有人愿意自己思考、记忆或推理。渐渐地，我们把大脑外包出去，失去了深度思考的习惯。身体上的懒惰同理：有了外卖软件和各种线上服务，许多人很少走路、做饭或活动，身体便和头脑一样闲置。\n诚然，科技也能让我们更有效率。但该受责备的不是工具，而是我们被动的依赖。因此，真正的问题不在于科技是否让我们变懒，而在于我们是掌控它，还是被它掌控。用得明智，它让我们自由；用得盲目，它让我们受奴役。",
