        "promptEn": "For this part , you are allowed 30 minutes to write an essay titled“Are people becoming addicted to technology?”.The statement given below is for your reference. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.\nNumerous studies claim that addiction to technology is real and it has the same effect on the brain as drug addiction.",
        "promptZh": "就「人们是否正在对科技上瘾」这一话题写一篇短文，表明并论证自己的看法。",
        "modelEssay": "Are people becoming addicted to technology? My answer is a definite yes. As numerous studies claim that addiction to technology is real, this problem deserves our serious attention.\n\nSigns of such addiction are everywhere in daily life. Many people check their smartphones the moment they wake up and keep scrolling short videos until midnight. While technology is designed to make life easier, an increasing number of us feel anxious once we are separated from our screens. As a result, real conversations, sleep and study are all disturbed, which shows that our reliance has quietly turned into dependence.\n\nIn my view, therefore, people are indeed getting hooked on technology. However, this does not mean we should abandon it. What matters is to use technology in a rational way, setting limits on screen time and leaving room for the real world.",
        "modelEssayZh": "人们正在对技术上瘾吗？我的回答是肯定的。既然大量研究都声称技术成瘾真实存在，这个问题就值得我们认真对待。\n这种上瘾的迹象在日常生活中随处可见。很多人一睁眼就摸手机，晚上刷短视频刷到半夜。尽管技术本是为了让生活更方便，越来越多的人一旦离开屏幕就感到焦虑。结果是，真实的交流、睡眠和学习都受到了干扰，这说明我们的依赖已经悄悄变成了成瘾。\n因此，在我看来，人们的确正在被技术‘套牢’。然而，这并不意味着我们应当抛弃它。关键在于理性地使用技术：给屏幕时间设定上限，也给现实世界留出一席之地。",
